Z||000004||CUTTER||05-31-2000||05:42 PM||||Could someone give me the specs of a stock 87GT and a stock 97 GSR V-Tech? I think I can take him because the 1/4 mile times are a little slower in the integra then in the 87GT's, Right?||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||05-31-2000||07:10 PM||||1994 Acura Integra GSR 0-60 in 7.1 seconds and the ¼-mile in 15.5. 1987 fiero GT 0-60 in 7.7 seconds and the 1/4-mile in 16 seconds flat bone stock.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||06-01-2000||01:43 AM||||Since you've got a slushbox, you're screwed.  You'd have to have a few more mods than you're running now in order to take him in an auto.  Most auto V6's are running in the 16's on a good day.  But you can always do the ricer blow-by after you lose!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||Bens88GT||06-02-2000||07:16 PM||||They're right, you're screwed. I know, because my 88GT is an auto as well, and I ALSO have a '99 Integra GS-R. The Fiero will beat the Integra off the line, but after about 40 mph he'll walk away from you.<P>And the Integra has VTEC, not V-Tech. V-Tech is a phone.||||reg||1
